        "answer": "The following table shows the total market value of Technology sector holdings for each portfolio, the total portfolio value, and the percentage of the portfolio represented by Technology holdings:\n\n| Portfolio Name | Tech Value | Total Portfolio Value | Tech Percentage |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Tech Innovation Fund | 1,565,292.50 | 1,565,292.50 | 100.00% |\n| Growth Equity Fund | 1,866,148.00 | 2,204,148.00 | 84.67% |\n| Total International Index Fund | 1,427,086.00 | 2,281,686.00 | 62.55% |\n| International Equity Fund | 346,888.00 | 734,928.00 | 47.20% |\n| Total Stock Market Index Fund | 3,093,520.00 | 6,622,340.00 | 46.71% |\n| Balanced Portfolio | 388,704.00 | 1,073,279.00 | 36.22% |\n| Emerging Markets Fund | 339,095.00 | 1,045,100.00 | 32.45% |\n| ESG Sustainable Fund | 272,978.00 | 1,007,228.00 | 27.10% |",
        "tools": [
          {
            "tool": "sql_query",
            "arguments": {
              "explanation": "Calculate the total market value of Technology sector holdings per portfolio, the total portfolio value, and the percentage of the portfolio value represented by Technology holdings. Only portfolios with Technology holdings are included.",
              "question": "For each portfolio, show the total value of Technology sector holdings and what percentage it represents of the total portfolio value",
              "sql": "WITH PortfolioValues AS (\n    SELECT \n        h.portfolio_id,\n        SUM(h.quantity * s.current_price) AS total_portfolio_value\n    FROM holdings h\n    JOIN securities s ON h.security_id = s.security_id\n    GROUP BY h.portfolio_id\n),\nTechValues AS (\n    SELECT \n        h.portfolio_id,\n        SUM(h.quantity * s.current_price) AS tech_value\n    FROM holdings h\n    JOIN securities s ON h.security_id = s.security_id\n    JOIN sectors sec ON s.sector_id = sec.sector_id\n    WHERE sec.sector_name = 'Technology'\n    GROUP BY h.portfolio_id\n)\nSELECT \n    p.portfolio_name,\n    tv.tech_value,\n    pv.total_portfolio_value,\n    ROUND((tv.tech_value / pv.total_portfolio_value) * 100, 2) AS tech_percentage\nFROM TechValues tv\nJOIN PortfolioValues pv ON tv.portfolio_id = pv.portfolio_id\nJOIN portfolios p ON tv.portfolio_id = p.portfolio_id\nORDER BY tech_percentage DESC;"
